For ICAcademy, I recommend building a professional course academy where each course contains modules, each module contains lessons, and every lesson can be configured as free or paid. The experience should feel like a modern learning platform, with a clear student journey and a well-organized instructor dashboard.

# ICAcademy — Course & Module System

## 1. Professional course structure

## Course

Course title, cover, description, instructor, pricing and learning outcomes.

Module 01 — Introduction

Module title, summary, sequence and completion requirements.

Lesson 1 — Welcome

Free preview · Video and notes

Free

Lesson 2 — Core concepts

Video, resources and exercises

Paid

Lesson 3 — Knowledge check

Quiz and assessment

Paid

Module 02 — Practical implementation

More lessons, projects, downloads and assessments.

The essential rule: a course contains modules, modules contain lessons, and each lesson has its own content, access rules and completion status.

## 2. Course access and pricing

I would build three distinct access levels so ICAcademy can support free education and paid premium content.

Free course

Students enroll without payment and access all published lessons, quizzes and resources included in the course.

Free enrollment

Paid course

Students see the course outline and purchase the course to unlock its protected modules and lessons.

Purchase required

Free preview + premium lessons

Allow selected lessons to be viewed for free, while the remaining content requires enrollment or payment.

Recommended model

This mixed-access approach is supported by established learning platforms, which offer preview lessons alongside protected premium content.&#x20;

