## 3. Admin dashboard — course creation flow

The course creator should have a step-by-step workflow instead of a single complicated form.

### 01

Course details

Title, slug, description, thumbnail, category, instructor and learning objectives.

### 02

Curriculum builder

Create modules, add lessons, reorder content and preview the complete outline.

### 03

Lesson editor

Add video, rich text, images, code examples, attachments, quizzes and assignments.

### 04

Access & pricing

Choose free or paid, set the price, define preview lessons and configure enrollment.

### 05

Course settings

Configure prerequisites, completion rules, certificates, publishing and optional scheduled releases.

### 06

Preview & publish

Validate required fields, preview the student experience and publish the course.

## 4. What each lesson should contain

Every lesson should have its own editor and settings.

| Field        | Purpose                                                |
| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------ |
| Lesson title | Clear name shown in the curriculum                     |
| Lesson type  | Video, article, code, quiz, assignment or resource     |
| Content      | Main lesson material                                   |
| Duration     | Estimated learning time                                |
| Access       | Free preview, enrolled students or premium restriction |
| Resources    | Downloads, links, attachments and code files           |
| Completion   | Manual completion, quiz pass or other defined rule     |
| Visibility   | Draft, published or scheduled                          |
| Order        | Position within its module                             |

