## 6. Important technical requirements

For a professional implementation, I would make these requirements mandatory:

- Server-side access control: hiding a locked lesson in the UI is not enough. The API must reject unauthorized requests for lesson content and protected resources.
- Reliable payment verification: unlock paid access only after the server verifies a successful payment; support payment retries and duplicate-event protection.
- Separate enrollment and purchase records: free enrollment and paid enrollment should use the same learning experience without confusing purchase status with progress.
- Progress tracking: store lesson completion and course progress per student.
- Flexible permissions: support course-wide pricing as well as individual free-preview lessons.
- Publishing workflow: drafts should not appear as published courses; changes should be validated before publication.
- Responsive course player: a persistent curriculum sidebar on desktop and a collapsible lesson list on mobile.
- Testing: verify free access, paid access, expired or revoked access, direct URL attempts, payment failures and lesson completion.

## 7. Recommended initial release

Start with course creation, modules, lessons, free/paid access, checkout integration, a student dashboard and progress tracking. Add certificates, scheduled lesson releases, discussion areas and advanced analytics once the core flow is reliable.

